    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26179" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lēgis-lātor</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lēgum-lātor</span></b>  (in
		class. authors usu. written separately; v. lator),
		ōris, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a law-giver, legislator</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noster legumlator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					34, 31</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 7, 8, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Decl. 329</span></i>; <i><span class="en">334</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legislator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 6, 5</span></i>
			, n. 3 <i>ext.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non satis in ea re legislatorem voluntatem suam
					verbis expressisse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gai. Inst. 3, 76 al.</span></i>
			</div>
